  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1134 PM CDT WED SEP 23 2026\n\nA few lingering showers are still ongoing in the far southeast\nthis evening. These will fade over the next few hours as easterly\nflow increases across the area. This will result in some\nisentropic lift through mid-morning, possibly lasting until noon.\nNumerical guidance is very pessimistic regarding rain chances\njust before dawn and through noon; however, model graphics show\nenough consensus to warrant a low confidence in light rain moving\neast to west through the morning. Most locations may only see a\ntrace, but a few could see minor accumulations. Even if it is\nonly a light drizzle, it will give the perception of light rain\nfalling. After noon, drier air works in from the east, starting\nanother dry spell, this time about 15 degrees cooler than the\nrecent heat wave. Highs will be in the upper 70s to low 80s\nthrough the rest of the week and into the weekend, making for\npleasant outdoor conditions.\n\n16",
